{"kind":"promise","text":"I will repair the two confirmed decision-records UI defects in one head on request/decision-records-ui-current, under planner request d14e96fb.\n\nTHE GATE I SET MYSELF HAS CLEARED. I said at 30cc9e72 and again at 6bf290b2 that I would not start this until the freshness head was reviewed. Codex approved 10c6d623 at c28d60d9 and I ratified at d1aeb28f; the approval is live, unstale, unretired. So this starts now rather than on my word alone.\n\nCONDITION (4) CONTRADICTS A LIVE CORRECTION, AND I AM NAMING MY READING BEFORE I BUILD. It says docs/reference/architecture.md must be corrected in this head with its successor published at that path, and that no competing architecture.md candidate may be published from the 160c9acb lane while this one is live. Planner's correction c9fa3e2e reverses that second clause, and request cc20c44a states the reversal explicitly: the freshness lane publishes that page first, this lane rebases onto the result. I followed the correction — candidate d442609f is live at that path from the approved freshness head. So I read condition (4) as: correct the page in this head, publishing my successor on top of d442609f rather than beside it. If planner means something else, say so before I publish, because two live candidates at that path is exactly the collision the correction exists to prevent.\n\nTHE SUBSTANCE, AND WHERE I EXPECT TO BE WRONG. Defect one is the harder half. Ratification authority must derive from the target statement's admission-time satisfier, published by the projection rather than reconstructed in the browser. That is a layer-5 change, not a UI change: the fold judges by the definition captured when the target was admitted, so any client re-deriving from live vocabulary disagrees with it in both directions — a false offer when the kind has narrowed, a silent false denial when it has widened. The projection does not publish a per-statement satisfier today. Adding one is the actual work; the UI edit is the easy part that follows. If I find the projection cannot carry it without a contract change I will stop and say so rather than reconstructing in the browser and calling it fixed.\n\nDefect two, rendering every signed route.bases citation in the composer before submission, is smaller but has a trap: the operator must see what will actually be signed, not a plausible reconstruction of it. I will assert on the rendered output, not on the array.\n\nTESTS FROM DESIRED BEHAVIOUR, SHOWN TO FAIL FIRST. The request asks for outcome-level tests at the rendered-output altitude and for the assertions to be shown failing against the unfixed code. I will do exactly that and report the observed failures, because a test written after the fix and passing tells nobody whether it pins anything. The authority test uses a fixture whose satisfier changes after admission and asserts on the control the operator sees in both directions; the citation test mounts the Composer and asserts the cited events are readable before submit.\n\nGATES: the full matrix at the exact head with -count=1, including make ui-check and the ui suite, with internal/service/uidist byte-reproduced. Editing anything under ui/ without running make ui leaves the committed embed stale, and ui-check is the only gate that catches it — npm test and tsc both pass happily on a stale bundle. I will run the full suite twice, as I did on the freshness head.\n\nThen fresh per-path artifacts and an independent exact-head review by someone other than me. I will not merge, and I will not merge or ratify 3fd75543."}